\end{align*}
In base 9, the digit 9 is equivalent to 10 in base 10. Therefore, the last column represents $A + A + 10$, and the second-to-last column represents $B + B + 10$. Since the sum of these columns is $B0_{9}$, we can write:
\[
\begin{align*}
A + A + 10 + B + B + 10 &= B0_{9} \\
2A + 2B + 20 &= B9_{10} \\
2A + 2B &= 99_{10} \\
A + B &= 49_{10}
\end{align*}
\]
The problem asks for $A \cdot B$. Since $A + B = 49$, we can factor this as $(A + B)(A - B) = 49 \cdot 2 = 98$. Therefore, the product $A \cdot B$ is 98.
$$
